      "method_path": [
        "BV = VC = sqrt(106), BC = 8",
        "cos(BVC) = (BV^2 + VC^2 - BC^2) / (2 * BV * VC)",
        "cos(BVC) = (106+106-64) / (2*106) = 148/212",
        "BVC = arccos(148/212) approx 0.798 (or 45.7 deg)"
      ],
      "accepted_alternatives": [
        "METHOD 2: Let M be midpoint of BC, BM = 4. Use right triangle BMV: sin(BVM) = 4/sqrt(106), BVC = 2 arcsin(4/sqrt(106)) approx 0.798.",
